{
  "_comment": "Dispatch offline Phase 5 hardening \u2014 THE signature image contract, shared by Laravel (App\\Services\\Terms\\SignatureImage) and the phone (TermsSignatureImage.swift). Both signing clients produce PNG only (signature_pad toDataURL image/png), so exactly one form is accepted: \"data:image/png;base64,\" + strict canonical base64 of a well-formed PNG within the limits below. Limits: both signing pages draw the pad at a pixel ratio of at most max_pad_ratio (3), and the decoded size covers an INCOMPRESSIBLE signature (raw RGBA, e.g. canvas read-back noise in privacy modes) on the largest such canvas (phone page at ratio 3, 1344x480 = 2,580,960 bytes raw); measured signature_pad output sits far inside it (largest: phone page at ratio 3, 219,340 bytes). Dimensions 4096x2048 and 4 MP. Vectors written independently with Python zlib/struct. Reasons: not_png_data_url, malformed_base64, too_large, not_png, dimensions_exceeded, undecodable. \"undecodable\" is decided by decoding the image (server: GD; phone: UIImage), not by the structural check.",
